        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-29T00:36:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, so, the motivation of these changes is paying for the 16 KB w/o sparsity changes (a small market segment, due to the issue in b/376814207). If these changes get in, then users get that, users fill up space, then the changes adding 16 KB w/o sparsity would be a real size increase on those devices, causing us not to be able to merge it.\n\nSo, we need to make sure all 4 changes happen in a release atomically, and the easiest way to do that is one at a time. If we wait until after the next merge deadline, we could start merging them one at a time. Though, being able to do it at once (and revert together) even if it is more errorprone or makes it more likely for a full topic revert is a bit easier than tracking branches/dates/etc..",
      "parentUuid": "11373356_52983c93",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 9,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "bcd0d12a9fea0d6005eac768b989a752062300e9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "23b621a5_d90d02de",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1018108
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-29T08:08:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see, this is about devices that have very little storage left. And while there are many things that can go wrong on such devices, it\u0027s reasonable to try not making it worse for them.\n\nHowever, submitting to AOSP does not really include the CL in the next ART Module release. So, we can submit one at a time and then make sure we cherry-pick them together to the release branch.\n\n(Unless you\u0027re trying to protect Beta users that fill up space but I would not worry about that particular population - they are getting a lot of more dangerous changes when upgrading to the next Beta.)",
      "parentUuid": "fb8ce2bb_2702def4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 9,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "bcd0d12a9fea0d6005eac768b989a752062300e9",
